  "solution": {
    "text": "We have : $30=2 \\times 3 \\times 5 .$ So, 2 can be assigned to either a or b or ci.e. 2 can be assigned in 3 ways. Similarly, each of 3 and 5 can be assigned in 3 ways. Thus, the number of solutions is $3 \\times 3 \\times 3=27$",
